#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4851cda0-b113-5476-8e09-cceada5f07f6" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "cecc0a5a-10be-59b9-a8c5-ae907679ed65" :question/math-academy-id "e-4474" :question/problem "Calculate the value of $2+ (-6).$" :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give \n\n$$\n2+ (-6) = 2-6.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we move $6$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](images/ed/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nWe end up at $-4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n2 + (-6) = -4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "498454ca-7ef2-57fb-aa4b-4884aed0c24e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Decimal"}] :question/id #uuid "f5138ecd-8e2e-5f83-a286-d770a53fba6f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4478" :question/problem "What is the value of $-1 + (- 2.5)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-1 + (- 2.5) = -1 - 2.5.\n$$\n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n\n$$\n-1 - 2.5 = -3.5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd8feed5-e1ee-5d1a-bba3-4fb2adee27ed" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "aa932148-f7fc-5e12-ad35-e9e90df25cc6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4484" :question/problem "Find the value of $-\\dfrac{2}{5} + \\left(- \\dfrac{3}{10}\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac 2 5 + \\left(-\\dfrac{3}{10}\\right) = -\\dfrac 2 5 -\\dfrac{3}{10} .\n$$\n\nNow, we need to convert the fractions to have the same denominator. To convert $-\\dfrac{2}{5}$ to have a denominator of $10,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n- \\dfrac{2}{5} = - \\dfrac{2 \\times 2}{5 \\times 2} = - \\dfrac{4}{10}\n$$\n\nNow, the subtraction problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{3}{10} & =-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the two fractions now have the same denominator, we can combine the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{-4-3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $-4 - 3$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/dd/dd96e6f3b2a3e35d0f792cb828ef905cfb0ea86b0962b017ceaa0630e4aba144.png)\n\nWe find that $-4-3=-7.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {-4 - 3} {10} = \\dfrac{-7}{10} = -\\dfrac{7}{10} .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "498454ca-7ef2-57fb-aa4b-4884aed0c24e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Decimal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28addabe-4e7b-5428-996d-bbd2705ac3b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444806} {:answer/id #uuid "507dfdb9-0cd7-5932-8c7d-12c1f95fca95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444811} {:answer/id #uuid "67dac6e0-cbfa-5b12-95a3-47db6eeb58ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444815} {:answer/id #uuid "6f23ceae-2b55-5e9c-975a-4db1133f2947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444817} {:answer/id #uuid "be1c0915-f500-5e07-b328-60da3be5475f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67dac6e0-cbfa-5b12-95a3-47db6eeb58ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444815} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a0a656-3346-573d-b4f8-1b43ee3ba445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1a479d0-fff3-5ce1-b03e-c90e28459585" :question/math-academy-id "q-101304" :question/problem "What is the value of  $9+(-5.5)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n9+(-5.5)=9-5.5.\n$$\n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n\n$$\n9-5.5=3.5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "498454ca-7ef2-57fb-aa4b-4884aed0c24e" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Decimal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1672c441-3685-546c-b7a6-44e9598ab827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444805} {:answer/id #uuid "2a1794ec-e0e4-5310-8b42-ba080bc3d470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444807} {:answer/id #uuid "622599ef-0615-50ac-af07-8dc9e9fc7fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444814} {:answer/id #uuid "a43e8c22-6b1b-5f17-81d2-f92d54c64990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444825} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb55062-1d7c-567b-832e-ea3ccf6e358a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdb55062-1d7c-567b-832e-ea3ccf6e358a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444829} :answer-field/id #uuid "52b99d3d-4dcb-5d15-b43d-c188a9b40d09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9cc8296-f82a-5b59-ab73-a756fc3da0a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128163" :question/problem "What is the value of  $4.7+(-2.5)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n4.7+(-2.5)=4.7-2.5.\n$$\n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n\n$$\n4.7-2.5=2.2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd8feed5-e1ee-5d1a-bba3-4fb2adee27ed" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e46888-3661-52b7-a84f-201e60473da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40e46888-3661-52b7-a84f-201e60473da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444810} :answer-field/id #uuid "95888e19-1242-5bc8-a7ff-63552a9743bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "17e6f69c-9289-5c2f-847c-503ec0fb9123" :question/math-academy-id "q-173782" :question/problem "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form, $\\frac{2}{3}+(-\\frac{4}{9})=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}+(-\\frac{4}{9})=\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we put the fractions over a common denominator of $9$ and combine the numerators, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{4}{9} & =\\frac{6}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}=\\frac{6-4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $6-4$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/4e/4ebf100b7da9bbada9145b4b5ea018cfee8ff2037307ca5023d6c2de54705fdd.png)\n\nWe find that $6-4=2.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-4}{9}=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4851cda0-b113-5476-8e09-cceada5f07f6" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ce8bdb3-5972-5a6b-905e-649b466ed368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444809} {:answer/id #uuid "555c9abd-386a-5aaf-a290-7c4f877b5e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444813} {:answer/id #uuid "82ac54f9-5cfc-5e36-b51e-d3a83b491819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444821} {:answer/id #uuid "88a3c421-aaf5-5ed8-8c43-248c1f03d80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444822} {:answer/id #uuid "ab510ebd-c938-5800-81e9-2a598d7aa486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88a3c421-aaf5-5ed8-8c43-248c1f03d80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444822} :answer-field/id #uuid "429a39e7-0900-5899-ac8a-99bd699da3c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "400c3acc-5e79-52be-941c-8ede9d67d05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1955" :question/problem "$2+(-5)=$" :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give $2+(-5)=2-5.$ \n\nThen, we move $5$ spaces to the left of $2$ on a number line.\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe end up at $-3.$ So, $2+(-5)=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd8feed5-e1ee-5d1a-bba3-4fb2adee27ed" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c085a6-ae35-5446-a9d4-f5599073a413" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444804} {:answer/id #uuid "7181e624-d73c-5c12-82b2-ebdd0c446fe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444818} {:answer/id #uuid "71abb7b2-24fe-5386-846c-d29251f1c081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444819} {:answer/id #uuid "9b88212e-44c8-5c0a-9dfa-9355dd0b993c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444824} {:answer/id #uuid "d28840ce-257e-593b-ac2f-5ded1891a387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71abb7b2-24fe-5386-846c-d29251f1c081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444819} :answer-field/id #uuid "a615bd8f-0f0f-5ad3-ae80-ed83e37ef67c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ba4fabf-8311-5600-bcfe-05b44a10e255" :question/math-academy-id "q-42864" :question/problem "What is  $\\text{ }-\\frac{1}{11}+(-\\frac{3}{11})?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we drop the parentheses and the addition sign, which gives\n\n$$\n\\text{ }-\\frac{1}{11}+(-\\frac{3}{11})=-\\frac{1}{11}-\\frac{3}{11}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since both fractions have a common denominator of $11$, we can combine the numerators, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{11}-\\frac{3}{11} & =\\frac{-1-3}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $-1-3$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/64/64d008419fd882c918e73b577956b3e36d3a32814fff62d495c0f75b7d107cd1.png)\n\nWe find that $-1-3=-4.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-1-3}{11}=\\frac{-4}{11}=-\\frac{4}{11}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444839 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4851cda0-b113-5476-8e09-cceada5f07f6" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ac01d11-7fca-5866-9f35-fc51aef94fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444808} {:answer/id #uuid "523ea15b-7817-5cc6-9723-b93a5c21253d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "140" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444812} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2385dd-e704-5a6f-a5a8-c37149fa46c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444816} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed42e4a-b79d-5685-a49e-233ca7338787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444820} {:answer/id #uuid "924f556a-1a02-506e-8aa9-357927ea6268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ac01d11-7fca-5866-9f35-fc51aef94fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444808} :answer-field/id #uuid "17c89d3f-1f1c-5a32-b35d-3f19c82047a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186444830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba9103c6-cd4f-5fe9-b177-f46928ef48cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-6127" :question/problem "What is $170+(-70)?$" :question/worked-solution "We drop the parentheses and the addition sign to give \n\n$$\n170+(-70)=170-70.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we carry out the subtraction as usual. This gives\n \n\n$$\n170-70=100.\n$$"}]}
